Please find the Q3 2021 inspection status for the ATU-100. All activities are being tracked against the current RBI intervals defined in QSCP-IP-ATU100 Rev 3, which specifies 3 years for Class 1 sour gas, regenerator overhead and rich amine, and 6 years for the remaining lines.

The current thickness data is based on the re-baseline survey of 150 CMLs conducted by Larkhall NDE Services Inc. as detailed in LNDE-RPT-20191001-027-R0. We are continuing to monitor these points to ensure remaining life calculations and next inspection dates remain within the class maxima.

Regards,  Jennifer Walsh

